Map key-order canonicalisation — CONTROL.

Same query and same two deliveries of the same logical stream as
map_key_order_count_over_time.txtar, except both deliveries carry a
byte-identical ResourceAttributes key order. One series either way, so this
fixture reports 1 with the canonicalisation and 1 without it. It exists to
pin the trigger fixture's discriminating variable: the two fixtures differ
only in the physical key order of the second row, so a regression that moves
the trigger while leaving this one still says "key order", not "seed shape"
or "window boundary".

-- query.logql --
count(count_over_time({job="api"}[5m]))
-- seed --
CREATE TABLE otel_logs (
    Timestamp DateTime64(9),
    Body String,
    SeverityText LowCardinality(String) DEFAULT '',
    SeverityNumber UInt8 DEFAULT 0,
    ResourceAttributes Map(String, String),
    LogAttributes Map(String, String)
) ENGINE = Memory;
INSERT INTO otel_logs (Timestamp, Body, SeverityText, ResourceAttributes) VALUES
    (toDateTime64('2025-12-31 23:59:00', 9), 'a', 'INFO', map('dc', 'eu', 'job', 'api')),
    (toDateTime64('2026-01-01 00:00:00', 9), 'b', 'INFO', map('dc', 'eu', 'job', 'api'));
-- expected_rows --
[
  ["", {}, "2026-01-01T00:00:01Z", 1]
]
